  "id": "COMPOUND:20808 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking 2-Ethyl-3-propylacrolein, (Z)- to Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions. This compound appears to act as a common intermediary in the targeting of H9, which is a target of three distinct compounds: Songorine, Gramideoxybenzoin F, and Communin B. All three of these compounds are implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a possible shared biological role in modulating this enzyme. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a plausible, albeit indirect, pathway through which 2-Ethyl-3-propylacrolein, (Z)- might influence Phosphodiesterase 6C. The mechanism likely involves the inhibition or modulation of H9, which in turn affects the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of H9 as a central node in the network, with multiple compounds acting through it to influence the same target. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
